prompt:
A real photograph of a small, cosy Tokyo apartment on a cold December evening, where four friends sit round a heated low table with a quilt, in a tall vertical picture, caught as it happens, as a friend standing in the kitchen doorway would take it with a good phone camera. Taken with a 24 mm lens at standing eye height, looking down a little at the low table and the friends around it, towards the window, everything in sharp focus. Warm light from a ceiling lamp and the steam of a hot pot; the textures of real woven straw, quilted cotton, wood, ceramic, steam, knitted wool, corduroy, paper, fur and skin. It looks exactly like a real phone photograph of real people: real skin with pores and small flaws, real hair, real cloth with its fine weave, natural light and the slight grain of a phone camera.

The first reference picture shows the young woman from the front, the second shows her from her side, the third shows her friend Yui, a Japanese woman of twenty-seven: the young woman's face, curly dark-brown hair and build, and Yui's face, short straight black bob and build, stay exactly as in them. Use them for the people only; here the young woman wears a plain mustard-yellow knitted sweater, and Yui a plain pale-grey knitted cardigan.

Every surface in the picture is plain: the quilt is plain dark-red cloth, the cushions are plain dark-blue, the bowls are plain white and plain dark blue, the cans are plain silver, the playing cards are plain white with plain blue backs, the books have plain single-colour spines, the television screen is dark, and the curtains are plain cream. Each object stands clearly on its own, with a band of bare table, bare tatami or bare wall around it, so that the eye can tell at once where everything is.

The picture is built in three bands, from the bottom edge to the top edge.

THE TABLE, across the lower half of the picture:
- the low square heated table stands on pale-green tatami; its top sits on a thick plain dark-red quilt that hangs down on all four sides to the floor; everyone's legs are under the quilt;
- in the middle of the table, a clay hot pot on a small portable gas burner, steaming, with slices of meat, white cabbage, mushrooms and tofu in the broth; around it, small white bowls, pairs of chopsticks, a plate of raw meat, a plate of green vegetables, a bowl of eggs, a basket of mandarin oranges, two plain silver cans of beer, a teapot and cups;
- on the corner of the table, a spread-out hand of playing cards face down;
- round the table on dark-blue cushions sit four friends: the young woman of the reference pictures on the left, so cosy that she has slid down under the quilt until only her head and shoulders are out, lying on her back on the tatami, laughing, a peeled mandarin orange held up above her face; Yui of the third reference picture at the far side, sitting upright, only her arm reaching across the table to hold a piece of meat out with long chopsticks towards her friend's mouth, laughing; the young cook Kenta, a Japanese man of twenty-two with spiky black hair, in a plain black hoodie, on the right, holding up two playing cards with a smug grin; and the landlady's son Sho, a Japanese man of twenty-two with neat short black hair, in a plain dark-blue sweater, in the foreground seen from behind, his shoulders and the back of his head;
- a grey tabby cat sleeps curled on the edge of the quilt.

THE ROOM, across the middle of the picture:
- on the left, a low wooden cabinet with a small television with a dark screen, and an acoustic guitar leaning against the wall beside it;
- on the right, a wooden bookshelf of books with plain coloured spines, a framed photograph of four friends on top of it, and a small green plant;
- a round wall clock with a plain white face above the bookshelf.

THE WINDOW, across the upper third of the picture:
- the window at the back, with plain cream curtains drawn half open; beyond the glass, the dark winter night, the lit windows of the neighbouring buildings and a few snowflakes falling;
- from the ceiling hangs a round lamp with a white shade, lit, glowing warm.

The room is small, warm and joyful: between the objects and the people, the same bare tatami, the same bare wood and the same plain cream walls.
